alse,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117075","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117075","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117075.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117075.patch","merged_at":"2026-06-19T17:12:22Z"},"body":"Alter vertical field-of-view bounds error conditions from between 1 and 179 inclusive to between 0 and 180 exclusive.\r\n\r\nThis is to allow for vertical viewing angles of less than one, for virtual broadcast productions and real world lens matching. Most 40x sports broadcast lenses have a sub one degree vertical viewing angle, as do most zoom lenses with extenders. At present, Godot cannot be used for many sports virtual productions that Unity or Unreal are used for due to the unnecessarily restrictive FOV lower bound.\r\n\r\nTested on 4.6, no attempt made to alter the editor property hint as it remains sensible for the majority of use cases.\r\n\r\n![fov-adjustment](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9fecf5e4-f40e-42f8-a1c7-438f1dd4f648)\r\n\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_ty